\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Your likely leadership style\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 The combination of 
\f1\b high humility + high ethical leadership + fairly high empathy
\f0\b0  points toward a leader who is likely to be seen as trustworthy, reasonable, and development-oriented.\
Your 
\f1\b Machiavellianism at 57
\f0\b0  adds an interesting counterweight. You may naturally think about:\
\'93What is really going on here?\'94\uc0\u8232 \'93Who wants what?\'94\u8232 \'93What incentives are shaping this behavior?\'94\u8232 \'93What is the most effective way to get this done?\'94\
That can be an advantage. Strategic awareness is not inherently unethical. In fact, good leaders need to understand organizational politics.\
The risk is that you may occasionally become 
\f1\b more politically calculating than you realize
\f0\b0 , particularly when you believe the outcome is justified. Your high humility and ethics can make this especially subtle: you may not experience yourself as manipulative because your intentions feel legitimate.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Likely biases\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 You may be vulnerable to a few predictable biases:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 \'93I know what is really happening.\'94
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 Your strategic orientation may make you good at seeing hidden motives\'97but it can also make you over-attribute political motives to ordinary disagreement, uncertainty, or incompetence.\

\f1\b \'93The outcome justifies the tactic.\'94
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 Even with high ethical standards, a pragmatic person can rationalize a tactic because the intended result is good.\

\f1\b \'93I don't need much credit.\'94
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 High humility can become under-claiming. You may genuinely care more about the team than recognition, but others still need clear attribution of responsibility and contribution.\

\f1\b \'93I'll handle it myself.\'94
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 Humility doesn't necessarily prevent over-responsibility. You may absorb difficult decisions or emotional labor rather than distribute it.\

\f1\b \'93Because I can see their perspective, I understand their position.\'94
\f0\b0 \uc0\u8232 Empathy can create a false sense of certainty. You can understand someone's feelings without knowing their actual motives or intentions.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

