\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 2. Top 3 risks to monitor\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Risk 1: \'93Justified manipulation\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Your Machiavellianism is high enough to make strategic influence a meaningful capability.\
The warning sign is not persuasion itself. It is when you start thinking:\
\'93They don't need to know why I'm doing this.\'94\
Watch for selective information, engineered choices, triangulation, indirect pressure, or deliberately withholding context because you believe disclosure would make the outcome harder.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Monitor:
\f0\b0  Am I influencing openly, or engineering the outcome?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 Risk 2: Empathy switching off under perceived unfairness\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Your empathy is a strength, but empathy is often 
\f1\b state-dependent
\f0\b0 .\
When someone violates trust or fairness, you may shift from understanding the person to understanding 
\f2\i why they deserve consequences
\f0\i0 . That can produce a sharper response than you intended.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Monitor:
\f0\b0  Does the severity of my response match the behavior, or my emotional reaction to it?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

